issue_context.body:
Use the latest `WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args)` to create the object `builder` and set it's `Properties` value through the `Host` property. 

For example, add a `data` element, but the value just set cannot be obtained in the `ConfigureContainer` and `UseServiceProviderFactory` methods. It will always be displayed here as the initial value.

However, in the past version (`.NET5`), it was normal through the `Host.CreateDefaultBuilder(args)`.

See the detailed code and screenshot below.

```cs
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// step1: add some share data
builder.Host.Properties.Add("data", "aspnetcore");

builder.Host.ConfigureContainer<IServiceCollection>((hostContext, services) =>
{
    // step2: the data is lost
    var data = hostContext.Properties; // the data is lost
});
```

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/22766122/132167358-4ce04123-beda-42de-9516-929dc19795ce.png)

```cs
var builder = Host.CreateDefaultBuilder(args);

// step1: add some share data
builder.Properties.Add("data", "aspnetcore");

builder.ConfigureContainer<IServiceCollection>((hostContext, services) =>
{
    // step2: the data is normal
    var data = hostContext.Properties; // the data is normal
});
```

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/22766122/132167687-f65934e6-a03e-4af4-9e7f-5d20745ce785.png)
